            <ArticleTitle>Leg ulcer management: how addressing a patient's pain can improve concordance.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>39-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Failure to carry out a comprehensive assessment of a patient with leg ulcers will often delay healing owing to non-concordance with treatment. This article uses a case study to encourage health professionals to improve care by focusing on each individual patient's perspective of pain and involving patients in planning a care regimen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
